@startuml

title The Acme demonstration: market data demand and subscription

participant "Acme party\n(its reports and curves)" as party
participant "ores.marketdata" as md
database "The catalogue\n(provider, source, vendor id,\nmapping, rate card)" as cat
database "The party's rows\n(subscription, route)" as rows
participant "The routed adapter\n(bloomberg-a, lseg-a, demo-a)" as adapter
participant "ores.marketdata.synthetic\n(the feed generators)" as sim

== The demonstration creates the party's two rows ==

party -> md : the acme_demo profile's\nsubscribe_market_data step
note right of md
  The step runs for every party of the
  tenant. A party the step names takes
  its own provider and source; a party
  it does not name takes the step's.
end note
md -> rows : put_subscription (party, provider,\ndisplay, non display, derived)
md -> rows : put_route (party, provider, source)
rows --> md : one subscription and one route\nfor each provider the party takes

== A run needs market data, so the party registers demand ==

party -> md : demand for an item\n(curve, spot, surface) at an as-of
md -> cat : which provider carries the item?
cat --> md : the provider and its vendor ids
md -> rows : which source serves this party\nfor that provider?
rows --> md : the route's source, and no other
md -> adapter : does this source serve the id?
adapter --> md : yes, it is in my announced universe
note right of md
  An id in the catalogue that an
  adapter does not announce cannot be
  demanded: the source screen says so
  rather than the run failing late.
end note
md -> sim : start the generator for the id
sim --> md : the generator runs

== The adapter publishes, and the service stores for this party ==

adapter -> md : marketdata.v1.ingress\n(one tick, in the vendor's own id)
md -> md : map the vendor id to the item,\nthen run the quality checks
md -> md : store one tick for this party
md --> party : the party's stream\n(marketdata tick)

== The bill follows the demand, not the price ==

md -> md : count the delivery against\n(the party, provider, item)
note right of md
  A simulated source carries a rate
  card of the same shape as a live one,
  so the demonstration shows the bill
  the same use would cost on a live
  source.
end note

@enduml
